          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**Finding — September 2025 cost period, Racine**\n\n- **Work order:** WO-2025-09-004 — **MO-25-09-1070** (Cooler Plate Pack)\n- **Source transaction:** TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070 (component issue; event CE-250904-0004)\n- **Amount:** 28,476,342 cents (**$284,763.42**)\n- **Event created:** **2025-09-30T19:15:00**\n- **Period entered Pending Close:** **2025-09-30T18:00:00**\n- **How late:** **75 minutes**\n- **Recorded accounting status:** **POSTED**\n- **Status consistent with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment?** **No.** Oracle’s policy says newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged or processed, subject to specified exceptions. This component-issue event is an INPUT event, not one of the listed exceptions, so POSTED is inconsistent with that treatment. *(Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF p. 233 / printed p. 225.)*\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed.",
